+## `bin/clean-workspaces.sh`
+
+Removes stale build workspaces: each immediate subdirectory of the workspace root whose
+newest file is more than the age threshold old. Symlinks in the root are ignored. Needs
+GNU `find` and Bash 4.4 or later.
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh [-n|--dry-run] [-r|--root DIR] [-d|--days N]
+```
+
+| Option | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `-r`, `--root DIR` | `workspaces` | Directory containing the workspaces (relative to the current directory). `/` is refused. |
+| `-d`, `--days N` | `7` | Remove workspaces older than `N` whole days. Must be a non-negative integer. |
+| `-n`, `--dry-run` | off | List what would be removed and remove nothing. |
+| `-h`, `--help` | | Show usage. |
+
+Examples:
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --dry-run                      # preview with the defaults
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --root /srv/ci/workspaces --days 14
+```
+
+Exit status: `0` success, `1` a removal failed, `64` bad usage, `66` root is not a directory.
